This rule documents how to write code for the current stack.

## Project Tech Stack

- Backend: NestJS + TypeScript (`apps/api`)
  - HTTP server: Fastify
  - ORM: TypeORM + PostgreSQL
  - Auth: JWT via `@nestjs/jwt` + `passport-jwt`
  - Validation: `class-validator` + `class-transformer`
  - Testing: Jest
- Frontend: Nuxt 4 + Vue 3 (`apps/pwa`)
  - Styling: Tailwind CSS
  - UI: shadcn-nuxt + Reka UI
  - Forms: HTML5 + vee-validate + zod
  - Charts: shadcn-vue charts (preferred)

## Backend Conventions (NestJS)

- Prefer thin controllers and move business logic into services.
- Use DTOs with `class-validator` for request validation.
- Use TypeORM entities and repositories; avoid inline SQL.
- Keep module boundaries clear: a module should export its service(s) and public providers only.
- Do not enable TypeORM `synchronize` in production; use migrations when schema changes are needed.
- Use explicit return types for public service methods.

## Frontend Conventions (Nuxt/Vue)

- Prefer `<script setup>` SFCs and Composition API.
- Keep components focused; extract shared logic into composables in `apps/pwa/composables`.
- Prefer shadcn-nuxt components before rolling custom UI.
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid custom CSS unless necessary.

## General Conventions

- Keep code small and readable; avoid clever abstractions.
- Match existing patterns and folder structure.
- Add comments only where logic is non-obvious.
